---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { REPO } from "../lib/site";
// The privacy policy of the app, the browser extension (ADR 0021), and this site. The
// Chrome Web Store listing of the extension links here. Keep it true to the code:
// docs/operations/browser.md, docs/adr/0015-automatic-updates.md, and
// docs/adr/0022-relay-sync.md.
const UPDATED = "2026-10-08";
---
<Page title="Privacy · apassy" description="What Apassy, its browser extension, and this site do with your data.">
  <main class="container">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your data stays on your Mac</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Apassy keeps your credentials on your Mac. There are no Apassy accounts, no analytics, and no ads. We never
        receive your passwords, your keys, or your vault. Updated {UPDATED}.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The Apassy app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your vault is a file on your Mac, encrypted with your passphrase (SQLCipher). Apassy reads it only on this Mac.</li>
        <li>
          The vault leaves your Mac only when you choose it: a backup file that you save, or sync through a folder that you
          pick (iCloud Drive, Dropbox, and others) or through the Apassy relay. What goes there is the encrypted vault
          file. Nobody can read it without your passphrase.
        </li>
        <li>
          Apassy checks for updates: it reads <code>https://apassy.wyderka.cc/latest.json</code> after the start and then
          every 6 hours. Like any web request, it carries the IP address of your Mac. You can turn the check off in Settings.
        </li>
        <li>The bouncer model runs on your Mac. Agent commands and your rules are not sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>The iPhone companion talks to your Mac on your local network only.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The browser extension</h2>
      <p>
        The Apassy extension for Chromium browsers fills, saves, and creates website logins from the Apassy app on the same
        Mac. It has no servers and makes no network requests.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What it reads.</strong> The address of the active tab, when you open the extension. The username and the
          password fields of the page, only when you click "Save this login". The extension does nothing on a page until you
          click its button.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Where the data goes.</strong> Only to the Apassy app on the same Mac, through the browser's native
          messaging. Apassy asks for Touch ID or your passphrase before it fills a login, saves one, or creates one. It
          never sends the data to us or to anyone else.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What it keeps.</strong> Nothing. It stores no data in the browser and never uses the clipboard. A
          password goes from the app into the page and is then dropped.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How the data is used.</strong> Only to fill, save, and create logins in your Apassy vault. It is not
          sold, not given to third parties, not used for ads, and not used to decide credit or loans.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Permissions.</strong> <code>nativeMessaging</code> to talk to the Apassy app, <code>activeTab</code>
          to read the address of the page that you are on after you click the button, and <code>scripting</code> to put
          the username and the password into the fields of that page.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site and its downloads are served by Cloudflare. It sets no cookies and has no analytics or trackers.</li>
        <li>
          Cloudflare keeps the usual request logs (IP address, time, address, browser) to run and protect the site. We use
          them only for that.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue on <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>GitHub</a>. Report a security problem privately,
        as <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}>SECURITY.md</a> says. The code of the app and the extension is
        public, so you can check each point above.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Page>

<style>
  main { max-width: 820px; padding-top: 72px; padding-bottom: 120px; }
  .head { padding-bottom: 36px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  h1 { margin-top: 12px; font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.05em; line-height: 1.02; }
  .lead { margin-top: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 48px; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .prose p { margin-top: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
  .prose ul { margin-top: 14px; padding-left: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .prose li { position: relative; padding-left: 22px; color: var(--muted); }
  .prose li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 0.7em; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--blue); }
  .prose li strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .prose a { color: var(--blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--blue) 35%, transparent); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .prose code { font-size: 0.88em; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--edge); color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
